            <ArticleTitle>Design, Synthesis, and Some Aspects of the Biological Activity of Mitochondria-Targeted Antioxidants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>760-777</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1134/S0006297917070021</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review summarizes for the first time data on the design and synthesis of biologically active compounds of a new generation - mitochondria-targeted antioxidants, which are natural (or synthetic) p-benzoquinones conjugated via a lipophilic linker with (triphenyl)phosphonium or ammonium cations with delocalized charge. It also describes the synthesis of mitochondria-targeted antioxidants - uncouplers of oxidative phosphorylation - based on fluorescent dyes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
